# ClawPilot — Heartbeat Checklist

## Purpose
The heartbeat is a lightweight, focused check-in that ensures nothing critical is being missed and no blockers are going stale.

## Schedule
- **Frequency:** Every 30 minutes during active hours (06:00–22:00 SGT)
- **Weekend:** Every 60 minutes
- **Off-hours:** Silent mode (urgent-only alerts)

## Heartbeat Checklist

### 1. Urgent Task Check
- [ ] Any tasks marked urgent in the last 30 minutes?
- [ ] Any deadlines approaching within 2 hours?
- [ ] Any pending confirmations older than 15 minutes?

### 2. Blocker Scan
- [ ] Any items stuck >4 hours without progress?
- [ ] Any mentions of blocked or stuck in recent messages?
- [ ] Any tasks awaiting external input that need follow-up?

### 3. Channel Health
- [ ] Telegram channels accessible and synced?
- [ ] Discord channels accessible and synced?
- [ ] Any connection errors or rate limit warnings?

### 4. Draft Queue Review
- [ ] Any unsent drafts pending >30 minutes?
- [ ] Any drafts that may now be stale?
- [ ] Priority ordering still valid?

### 5. Confirmation Status
- [ ] Any pending user confirmations?
- [ ] Any time-sensitive decisions awaiting input?

## Heartbeat Output Format

[HEARTBEAT] {timestamp} SGT
Urgent items: {count}
Stale blockers: {count}
Pending confirmations: {count}
Status: {clear|attention_needed|urgent}

## Escalation Rules

| Condition | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Stale blocker >8 hours | Flag for immediate review |
| Urgent item >1 hour unaddressed | Highlight prominently |
| Channel disconnected >5 minutes | Alert with recovery steps |
| Confirmation pending >1 hour | Gentle reminder |

## What Heartbeat Does NOT Do
- Send unsolicited messages
- Clear items from queues
- Make decisions on behalf of Mira
- Override confirmation requirements

## Notes
- Heartbeat is informational; all actions still require confirmation
- Run silently; only report when issues are detected
- Log heartbeat results to memory for pattern tracking

---
*Heartbeat version: 1.0 | Active: 2026-04-14*
ENDFILE

